        "Upstream stable is 1.4.12; the candidate stays 1.1.20 because 1.4.12 is not yet captured into Surface. A hermetic linux-x64 Rosetta farm of 1.4.12 runs end to end with the fix from Rosetta commit a6fbaadfbc3b3d9f7daa3ba64779383542aa5083 (Gemini mock follows the declared run_command schema; vibefield/rosetta#39, merged as 4282c44276d070958fbc442ca7a5b7021354aa5e), but importing it still needs: (1) a 1.4.12 writer document extracted from the 1.4.12 binary's FileDescriptorSet, since the only protobuf grammar is the 1.2.9 extraction and Rosetta pins the newest farmed release with writer evidence; (2) Rosetta antigravity raw types and goldens for the transcript drift (run_command results are recorded as GENERIC steps with no exit_code, PLANNER_RESPONSE carries input/cache_read/output token counts, CHECKPOINT no longer appears, run_command arguments are CommandLine/toolSummary/WaitMsBeforeAsync); (3) adapter rework, because tool results are correlated by the RUN_COMMAND step type and exit_code and would stay unresolved on 1.4.12; and (4) the Surface census harness re-run for 1.4.12 on all four platforms."
      ]
